    "passage": "During the blueberry season, this delightful little fruit captivates many people in Taiwan. They can be readily [[1]] at not only convenience stores but also online outlets. From ice cream and smoothies to tarts and cheesecake, blueberries are practically everywhere, seemingly [[2]] an essential part of the local culinary scene.\nCertain key considerations will help one become a successful blueberry farmer. Firstly, selecting suitable blueberry varieties is important because different varieties require different soils and climates. [[3]], both “Rabbiteye” and “Southern Highbush” flourish in Taiwan’s typical mild springs and humid summers and produce better yields than others. Also, while blueberries require ample water during their growth, excessive [[4]] can damage their roots and cause them to rot. It is thus essential to adjust watering frequency wisely. Finally, blueberries must be pruned diligently in order to [[5]] their growth and health. It is clear that only with sufficient effort and patience can high-quality blueberries be successfully planted.",
